wifi: brcmfmac: send action frames on the right channel (6.12 backport)

Backport of the mgmt_tx channel hunk of upstream f2d7c3c380bf, which
rpi-6.12.y and 6.12 stable lack. brcmf_cfg80211_mgmt_tx() treats the
BRCMF_C_GET_CHANNEL result as a frequency and converts it again, so an
NL80211_CMD_FRAME without a frequency is sent on a bogus channel. Use
the channel number: the requested channel's hw_value, or the firmware's
current channel as it is.

Not part of the upstream series (wireless-next already has it); carried
for the 6.12 Pi kernels only. Drop it when the image kernel has
f2d7c3c380bf.

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
@@ -5605,12 +5605,13 @@
 		/* Add the channel. Use the one specified as parameter if any or
 		 * the current one (got from the firmware) otherwise
 		 */
-		if (chan)
-			freq = chan->center_freq;
-		else
+		if (chan) {
+			chan_nr = chan->hw_value;
+		} else {
 			brcmf_fil_cmd_int_get(vif->ifp, BRCMF_C_GET_CHANNEL,
 					      &freq);
-		chan_nr = ieee80211_frequency_to_channel(freq);
+			chan_nr = freq;
+		}
 		af_params->channel = cpu_to_le32(chan_nr);
 		af_params->dwell_time = cpu_to_le32(params->wait);
 		memcpy(action_frame->data, &buf[DOT11_MGMT_HDR_LEN],
